, 0.019707013, -0.019588592, 0.0021756412, 0.020812217, 0.0097310105, 0.010142994, -0.021562846, 0.012859692, 0.028529733, 0.013072244, -0.0077472175, -0.020042738, 0.011053581, 0.006921237, 0.01128276, -0.009386545, 0.0025770955, 0.007695556, 0.02583666, 0.009135575, 0.027799005, 0.014442335, 0.0024113297, -0.005875388, -0.017548688, 0.01094015, 0.026823735, 0.011029112, 0.011104453, -0.014777203, -0.0048294156, -0.007418227, 0.018255252, -0.018896878, 0.009321178, -0.0194612, -0.010601946, 0.008109294, 0.021281337, -0.007384959, -0.010959366, 0.0037737188, 0.0013710425, 0.00873539, -0.00038871868, -0.015044128, -0.016694486, 0.0034232738, -0.0119533455, -0.024431936, -0.0077605764, -0.014170148, 0.0006951291, 0.0033563427, 0.011506537, -0.006786865, 0.016585946, -0.0019746174]}}}, {'index': {'_index': 'chunks', '_id': 'chunk_116bfc76-d9ca-4164-b677-253e452eb49a_4', 'status': 400, 'error': {'type': 'mapper_parsing_exception', 'reason': "failed to parse field [embedding] of type [knn_vector] in document with id 'chunk_116bfc76-d9ca-4164-b677-253e452eb49a_4'. Preview of field's value: 'null'", 'caused_by': {'type': 'illegal_argument_exception', 'reason': 'Vector dimension mismatch. Expected: 768, Given: 3072'}}, 'data': {'source_type': <SourceType.UPLOADED_FILE: 'uploaded_file'>, 'source_id': '116bfc76-d9ca-4164-b677-253e452eb49a', 'source_name': 'Bloomberg QRT Article.pdf', 'content': 'Hard Lessons\nAs well as lucky timing as investors chased around for multistrats, QRT has also\nbenefited from not starting from scratch. It began life on its own as a mature firm with\nan established model led by executives who’d run large businesses and suffered ups\nand downs, including one of history’s biggest trading scandals.\nToward the end of a more than 18-year stint at SocGen, Morlat was one of the bosses of\nKerviel, the rogue trader who’d amassed 50 billion euros in positions in European stock\nfutures using fake hedges and false documents that cost the bank 4.9 billion euros in\n2008. While an internal report didn’t blame anyone senior at the desk where Kerviel\nworked, he resigned.\nJain, then at Credit Suisse, wooed Morlat to join him there to head its proprietary\narbitrage trading for Europe and Asia. The Frenchman’s team spent much of its life as\npart of a little-known business deep within the bank’s stock-trading arm. Known as the\nSystematic Market-Making Group, or SMG, traders used the lender’s money and\ncomplex algorithms for speculative bets.\nDespite crackdowns on banks funding their own trading after the financial crisis, some\npersisted and SMG remained an important but rarely discussed part of Credit Suisse.\nThat changed in late 2016 when the lender moved the unit into its asset-management\narm, where it would try to raise outside money.\nThe era of SMG was ending — Qube’s was just beginning.\nQRT spun out of Credit Suisse on Jan. 1, 2018 as part of a management buyout with\nabout 100 people, including current Chief Risk Officer Christina Wilgress and Chief\nOperating Officer Stuart Brown. Some of the world’s largest investors backed the launch\nand have topped up their investments, people familiar say.\nHedge funds typically begin with one or two people and expand. “What QRT started as\nis, ‘let’s build something that’s sustainable for a larger group of people’ rather than, ‘hey,\nit’s based on one individual’s trading talent and let’s see what we can do’,” Dainton says.\nQRT staff are among its biggest investors.\nWhile specialist algorithmic-trading firms such as Alex Gerko’s XTX Markets are also\npiling into the data-center craze, in Finland in his case, it remains to be seen whether\nthe multistrat hedge funds follow QRT’s lead. It wants the Icelandic site to be up and\nrunning within six months.\nAmid a fierce war for talent — and as an industry once ruled by mavericks becomes\ninstitutionalized — there may be something too in the comparative stability at Morlat\nand Laizet’s outfit. The 14 partners and five core investors the firm started out with\nremain loyal.', 'start_pos': None, 'end_pos': None, 'bbox': {'page': 5, 'x': 0.0, 'y': 0.0, 'width': 595.32, 'height': 841.92, 'selector': None, 'xpath': None, 'offset': None, 'line_start': None, 'line_end': None, 'char_start': None, 'char_end': None}, 'metadata': {'page_number': 5, 'page_width': 595.32, 'page_height': 841.92, 'has_embedding': True}, 'id': 'chunk_116bfc76-d9ca-4164-b677-253e452eb49a_4', 'embedding': [-0.017667834, -0.01866084, -0.026554175, -0.07990953, 0.025808692, -0.017796544, 0.015748668, -0.00016861765, -0.005153787, 0.0106441295, -0.026712194, -0.0028167106, 0.029254567, 0.009663008, 0.1442626, 0.034976903, 0.003960022, 0.0024254238, 0.006376845, 0.011017982, 0.016525151, -0.0069843633, 0.006285742, -0.006758762, 0.007937287, -0.021890532, -0.019507864, 0.0052421396, 0.015366355, -0.011483626, 0.0061276373, 0.020257918, -0.0035287784, 0.029244345, -0.011192846, 0.005995222, 0.004059834, -0.032550078, -0.016975356, 0.038090426, 0.0007080094, -0.008494238, -0.00074878684, 0.026799401, -0.030941397, -0.028140161, 0.0076868553, -0.028366143, 0.0031044318, 0.03478373, -0.013623173, -0.0020570096, 0.012341174, -0.16426393, 0.011304855, 0.018467579, 0.0055382587, -0.01743948, 0.020636035, 0.029478373, 0.002556836, 0.009473187, 0.004983701, -0.014665144, -0.02743561, -0.038988832, 0.003750165, -0.00971746, 0.0068013878, -0.0013937466, 0.016851464, 0.0036952167, -0.020321386, -0.013487869, 0.017399548, -0.021291047, 0.006590924, 0.01402695, -0.008644244, 0.012666441, 0.0076606194, -0.009237477, 0.025412938, -0.0041563767, -0.019442, 0.009860714, -0.008639892, -0.0025203105, 0.03691174, -0.012252002, 0.002083263, -0.02349307, 0.0023051894, -0.012687892, 0.022842497, 0.0035304874, 0.018392645, 0.033900917, 0.0030242894, -0.015454365, -0.01575162, -0.06265991, -0.015548811, 0.00715176, -0.002812314, -0.01799313, 0.0013275796, 0.007956469, -0.014697198, 0.007106566, 0.0349704, 0.000579927, -0.027546532, 0.0064516226